<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferdinand II of Aragon</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferdinand II of Aragon was king of Aragon whose marriage to Isabella of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> united the two crowns. Together they completed the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> in 1492, sponsored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Columbus</a>'s voyage and expelled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a>, laying the foundations of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferdinand-ii-of-aragon.jpg" alt="Ferdinand II of Aragon" width="313" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michael Sittow · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Michel_Sittow_004.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
